# Special Notes in Code

When a requirement, constraint, or non-obvious behavior is **especially emphasized** (product note, SSR/auth caveat, stacking/layout contract, "do not change", cross-page global behavior), **document it in the code** — not only in chat or docs.

## Where to comment

| Location | Use for |
|----------|---------|
| Component / route (TSX) | Placement, global vs page-local, SSR vs client split |
| Module / server function (TS) | Auth, cookies, PKCE, data flow exceptions |
| CSS Modules / `global.css` | z-index, bleed, fixed layers, stacking contexts |

## Style

- Comments in **English** (same as source code).
- Explain **why** and **what must not change**, not what the line literally does.
- Prefer a short block comment above the relevant block; use `/** */` for exported APIs when the contract matters.
- Do **not** comment every line; only decisions that are easy to break or easy to misunderstand.

## Examples

```tsx
// Global fixed mesh — all routes share this; do not mount per-page HeroBackground.
<HeroBackground fixed />
```

```ts
// OAuth PKCE: exchange on the server so the code verifier cookie from sign-in is available.
const { error } = await supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)
```

```css
/* Stacking: fixed background z-index 0; header 20; main content 1. */
.appShell {
  isolation: isolate;
}
```

## Agent workflow

When implementing or restoring an emphasized behavior, add or update the matching comment in the same change. If you move logic (e.g. root → page), move the comment too.
